Z||000000||WisconsinGT||05-07-2000||08:28 PM||||This is the second tine it has happened. For some unexplainable reason after parking my 88, I go into the house, get a few things then get back into the car. When I turn the key hothing happenes. I have power. (stereo, Windows work.) So I go inside, wait for about 1 hour then come back out. The car starts right up. Anyone have any clues on what would cause this? Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||Oreif||05-07-2000||11:09 PM||||WI-GT, Sounds like you need to replace the starter. When it gets hot from engine running it stops working. Let it cool down it works fine! Actually it is the starter solinoid on the starter that is going bad.<BR>NAPA use to sell the solinoid (sometimes called a bendix) and they had normal and high temp. The high temp ones last forever!<BR>I bought one 4 years ago but don't know if they are still available. <p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 05-07-2000).]||||reg||1
